From f4a5e61acd7c54d646497345daf44c19be258324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2025 10:50:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 681/913] plat-stm32mp1: add message when error occur in
 psci_system_suspend

A information message is displayed in OP-TEE in psci_system_suspend
function but only on success, for example

I/TC: Enter cstop mode 2
I/TC: Resumed

Add a error message to report an issue and suspend request,
for example when Standby is not really performed, but limited to Stop mode.

I/TC: Enter cstop mode 5
E/TC:0   __psci_system_suspend:397 Resumed with error (-1)

It is important to have this information, because the issue is reported
to Linux in PSCI result and the suspend request failed with strange trace:

echo: write error: Invalid argument

For the request:

echo mem > /sys/power/state

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 3dd398c14e548d6217cb4968ef40fa6c01fb741b plat-stm32mp1: add message when error occur in psci_system_suspend]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I3fe2972cc972d10465a40b22f8ffb4718a9a5549
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/494416
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
index 5e82f1bf8..1db5e5045 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
@@ -396,6 +396,7 @@ uint32_t __weak __psci_system_suspend(uintptr_t entry,
 		IMSG("Resumed");
 		return PSCI_RET_SUCCESS;
 	}
+	EMSG("Resumed with error (%d)", ret);
 
 	return PSCI_RET_INTERNAL_FAILURE;
 }
